---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import FinalCTA from "../components/FinalCTA.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Atlas — founder-led project intelligence"
  description="Atlas is a founder-led service bringing business intelligence and information-monitoring experience to UK commercial HVAC project research."
  ><div class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="breadcrumb" href="/">← Back to Atlas</a><div class="eyebrow">
        About Atlas
      </div><h1>Good research.<br />A direct relationship.</h1><p class="lead">
        Focused project intelligence for UK commercial HVAC contractors who want
        to spend their time on the right opportunities.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div><div class="section">
    <div class="container article-grid">
      <article class="article">
        <section>
          <h2>Founder-led project intelligence</h2><p>
            Atlas is built by a software engineer with professional experience
            in business intelligence and information-monitoring workflows, now
            focused on helping UK commercial HVAC contractors identify projects
            worth pursuing.
          </p><p>
            The service applies that research discipline to a practical
            question: which upcoming commercial projects deserve a closer look
            from your business?
          </p>
        </section><section>
          <h2>Context makes the difference</h2><p>
            A project announcement is a starting point. Its usefulness depends
            on the scope, timing, organisations involved and whether there is a
            realistic route to a commercial conversation.
          </p><p>
            Atlas brings those pieces together and makes the unknowns explicit.
            Each brief should help you choose a next step, rather than leave you
            with another list to investigate.
          </p>
        </section><section>
          <h2>Built with founding contractors</h2><p>
            The four-week founding pilot is an opportunity to test the service
            against your coverage, capabilities and priorities. You work
            directly with the person reviewing the research and can explain what
            makes an opportunity useful to you.
          </p><p>
            At the end, continue only if the intelligence has been useful. There
            is no long-term commitment.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article><aside class="sidebar">
        <div class="eyebrow">Our approach</div><h2>Focused by design.</h2><ul
          class="checks"
        >
          <li>Commercial HVAC relevance</li><li>
            Personally reviewed research
          </li><li>Clear facts and open questions</li><li>
            A practical next action
          </li>
        </ul><a class="text-link" href="/sample-opportunity/"
          >Read the sample <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div><FinalCTA /></BaseLayout
>
